IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lpc-dates`
IMPORT `lpc-core`

-- Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA), Schedule 3 -- THE CLIENT'S SEAT: the person who retains a law practice (a
-- solicitor's firm, an incorporated legal practice, a barrister) for a claim or other matter and has to pay for it,
-- for example someone injured who signs a no win, no fee agreement. Every question is asked as that person would ask
-- it, from facts that person can state; the court's and the law practice's judgments are asked as conditions. The rules
-- are in lpc-core.l4; this module restates none of them.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (the Act at version 1.9.2026, the
-- Legal Practitioners Regulations 2014 at version 1.7.2020; unauthorised RTF renderings). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE
-- ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The client's questions about legal costs`

§§ `Does the South Australian costs law apply to my matter (cll 3-5)`

@export Do the South Australian rules on legal costs and costs agreements (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 Schedule 3) apply to my matter (Schedule 3 cll 3, 4, 5)?
GIVEN `where I first instructed`          IS A `Where first instructed` @desc Where you first gave the law practice instructions in this matter (in person, by post, phone, email or otherwise): in South Australia, in another Australian jurisdiction, or it cannot be determined where
      `the day I first instructed`        IS A DATE    @desc The day you first instructed the law practice in this matter
      `the work is mainly in SA`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal work is or will be done wholly or mainly in South Australia
      `the matter is connected with SA`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter has a substantial connection with South Australia: for example you live in South Australia, the law practice practises mainly there, or the work concerns land or court proceedings there (reg 58)
      `I accepted an offer that it apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you accepted (in writing or by conduct) the law practice's written offer that the South Australian costs rules apply to the matter
      `I gave notice that it apply`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you told the law practice in writing that you require the South Australian costs rules to apply
      `I was told of my right to notify`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice told you (under another jurisdiction's law) of your right to give such a notice
      `the day I was told`                IS A DATE    @desc The day it told you of that right (any day if it did not)
      `the day of my notice`              IS A DATE    @desc The day you gave your written notice (any day if you gave none)
      `the matter is connected elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is mainly done in, or the matter is substantially connected with, another Australian jurisdiction
      `I chose the other law`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you agreed with the law practice, or told it in writing in time, under that other jurisdiction's law, that its costs rules apply
GIVETH AN `Application answer`
`Does Schedule 3 apply to my matter` MEANS
    `does Schedule 3 apply (cll 3, 4, 5)` `where I first instructed` `the day I first instructed` `the work is mainly in SA` `the matter is connected with SA` `I accepted an offer that it apply` `I gave notice that it apply` `I was told of my right to notify` `the day I was told` `the day of my notice` `the matter is connected elsewhere` `I chose the other law`

§§ `Being told the costs (Part 3)`

@export Must my lawyer's firm (the law practice) give me written disclosure of its legal costs, or does an exception apply (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cll 9, 10, 11, 12, 13; reg 60)?
GIVEN `my lawyer is a barrister engaged for my matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lawyer you are asking about is a barrister engaged for your matter (usually by your solicitor)
      `my own law practice retained this one for me`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this law practice was retained for you by your own law practice (for example a firm of agents or a second firm)
      `the likely total legal costs`                   IS A NUMBER  @desc The total legal costs in the matter that are likely, in dollars, excluding disbursements (court fees, experts and the like) and excluding GST
      `I waived further disclosure`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a costs disclosure from this law practice in the previous 12 months and then agreed in writing to waive your right to further disclosure
      `a principal decided it was not warranted`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a principal of the law practice decided, on reasonable grounds, that further disclosure was not warranted (relevant only if you waived)
      `the kind of client I am`                        IS A `Kind of client` @desc What kind of client you are: an individual (or a business or body not listed); a law practice or legal practitioner; a public company or other large or foreign company; a financial services licensee; a liquidator, administrator or receiver; a large professional partnership; a joint venture company or group of the kind the Act describes; a Minister, government department or public authority; or a corporation held mostly for the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory
      `my costs were agreed by tender`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal costs, or how they are calculated, were agreed as a result of a tender process
      `I will not have to pay`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you will not be required to pay the legal costs and they will not otherwise be recovered (for example pro bono work)
GIVETH A `Disclosure answer`
`Must my law practice disclose its costs to me` MEANS
    `must the law practice disclose its costs (cll 9-13)` `my lawyer is a barrister engaged for my matter` `my own law practice retained this one for me` `the likely total legal costs` `I waived further disclosure` `a principal decided it was not warranted` `the kind of client I am` `my costs were agreed by tender` `I will not have to pay`

@export My law practice did not tell me something about its costs that it had to: what does that mean for me (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cl 18)?
GIVEN `it failed to disclose`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice failed to disclose to you anything Part 3 of Schedule 3 required (the basis of its costs, an estimate, your rights, an uplift fee estimate, a settlement estimate, a substantial change, and so on)
      `only because the other firm did not tell it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether its only reason was that a law practice it retained for you failed to give it the information (usually no)
      `I entered a costs agreement`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you entered a costs agreement with this law practice
      `the costs have been adjudicated`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court (or its Registrar) has adjudicated the costs under Part 7
GIVETH A `Failure to disclose answer`
`What follows from my law practice's failure to disclose costs` MEANS
    `what follows from a failure to disclose (cl 18)` `it failed to disclose` `only because the other firm did not tell it` `I entered a costs agreement` `the costs have been adjudicated`

@export Can my law practice charge me for a written report on my matter or on my costs so far (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cl 19)?
GIVEN `the report I want` IS A `Kind of report` @desc The report you ask for: a written report of the progress of the matter, or a written report of the legal costs incurred to date or since the last bill
GIVETH A `Report charge answer`
`Can I be charged for a report from my law practice` MEANS
    `may the law practice charge for the report (cl 19)` `the report I want`

§§ `Costs agreements (Part 5)`

@export Can my costs agreement for this matter be a conditional (no win, no fee) agreement (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cll 25(1), (2), 26(1a))?
GIVEN `my matter` IS A `Kind of matter` @desc The kind of matter: a criminal matter; one about child protection, custody, guardianship or adoption; proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975; proceedings under the Child Support (Assessment) Act 1989; proceedings under the Migration Act 1958; or another matter (for example a personal injury, compensation or other civil claim)
GIVETH A `Conditional matter answer`
`Can I have a no win no fee agreement for my matter` MEANS
    `may the agreement be conditional for this matter (cl 25(2))` `my matter`

@export Can my costs agreement make me pay an uplift fee (extra costs if I win) (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cll 1, 25(2), 26)?
GIVEN `my agreement is conditional`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement makes payment of some or all of the legal costs conditional on a successful outcome (no win, no fee)
      `my matter`                    IS A `Kind of matter` @desc The kind of matter: criminal; child protection, custody, guardianship or adoption; Family Law Act proceedings; Child Support (Assessment) Act proceedings; Migration Act proceedings; or another matter
      `my matter is litigious`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter involves, or is likely to involve, starting or defending proceedings in a court or tribunal
      `the risk is significant`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the risk of your claim failing, and of your having to meet your own costs, is significant (relevant only to a litigious matter)
GIVETH AN `Uplift answer`
`Can my costs agreement include an uplift fee` MEANS
    `may the agreement provide for an uplift fee (cl 26)` `my agreement is conditional` `my matter` `my matter is litigious` `the risk is significant`

@export What is the most uplift fee my lawyer may charge me in a litigious matter under a no win, no fee agreement (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cl 26(4)(b))?
GIVEN `the legal costs otherwise payable` IS A NUMBER @desc The legal costs you would otherwise pay under the agreement, in dollars, excluding disbursements and excluding the uplift fee itself
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most uplift fee in a litigious matter` MEANS
    `the most uplift fee in a litigious matter (cl 26(4)(b))` `the legal costs otherwise payable`

@export Can my lawyer charge me a percentage of my compensation or settlement (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cll 27, 29(5))?
GIVEN `it is a share of what I recover`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you pay the law practice (or part of it) is calculated by reference to the amount of an award or settlement, or the value of property recovered
      `it adopts an applicable scale`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that part of the agreement simply adopts an applicable court scale of costs
GIVETH A `Contingency answer`
`Can my lawyer charge a percentage of my compensation` MEANS
    `is the fee a prohibited contingency fee (cl 27)` `it is a share of what I recover` `it adopts an applicable scale`

@export Is my costs agreement with my lawyer valid, or void (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cll 24, 25, 26, 27, 29(1), 51)?
GIVEN `who the agreement is between`    IS A `Parties to the agreement` @desc Who made the agreement: you and the law practice you retained; you and a law practice your law practice retained for you; your law practice and a law practice it retained for you; or the law practice and someone who owes it your costs (an associated third party payer)
      `the kind of client I am`         IS A `Kind of client` @desc What kind of client you are: an individual (or a business or body not listed); a law practice or legal practitioner; a public company or other large or foreign company; a financial services licensee; a liquidator, administrator or receiver; a large professional partnership; a joint venture company or group of the kind the Act describes; a Minister, government department or public authority; or a corporation held mostly for the Crown
      `my costs were agreed by tender`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal costs, or how they are calculated, were agreed as a result of a tender process
      `it is in writing`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement is written or evidenced in writing
      `I accepted it by conduct`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you accepted a written offer by conduct (for example by giving instructions) rather than in writing
      `the offer said how to accept`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the written offer clearly stated that it was an offer to enter a costs agreement, that it could be accepted in writing or by conduct, and what conduct would accept it
      `it excludes adjudication`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement says the costs are not subject to adjudication by the Supreme Court
      `it is conditional`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether payment of some or all of the costs depends on a successful outcome (no win, no fee)
      `my matter`                       IS A `Kind of matter` @desc The kind of matter: criminal; child protection, custody, guardianship or adoption; Family Law Act proceedings; Child Support (Assessment) Act proceedings; Migration Act proceedings; or another matter
      `it defines success`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a conditional agreement sets out the circumstances that count as a successful outcome
      `it is in plain language`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is in clear plain language
      `I signed it`                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you signed it
      `it mentions independent advice`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it states that you were told of your right to get independent legal advice before entering it
      `its cooling-off business days`   IS A NUMBER  @desc How many clear business days of cooling-off (when you may end it by written notice) the agreement gives; 0 if none
      `it has an uplift fee`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it provides for an uplift fee (extra legal costs payable if you succeed)
      `the uplift basis is set out`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the basis for calculating the uplift fee is separately identified in it
      `the uplift is estimated`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it contains an estimate (or a range of estimates with the major variables) of the uplift fee
      `my matter is litigious`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter involves, or is likely to involve, court or tribunal proceedings
      `the risk is significant`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the risk of the claim failing, and of your having to meet your own costs, is significant
      `the uplift fee`                  IS A NUMBER  @desc The uplift fee, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the costs otherwise payable`     IS A NUMBER  @desc The legal costs otherwise payable, in dollars, excluding disbursements and the uplift fee
      `it is a share of what I recover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any amount you pay is calculated by reference to an award, a settlement or the value of property recovered
      `it adopts an applicable scale`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that part simply adopts an applicable court scale of costs
GIVETH A `Validity answer`
`Is my costs agreement void` MEANS
    `is the costs agreement void (cll 24-27, 29)` (`Costs agreement` WITH
        `parties`                                IS `who the agreement is between`
        `in writing or evidenced in writing`     IS `it is in writing`
        `accepted by conduct`                    IS `I accepted it by conduct`
        `the offer states what clause 24(4) requires` IS `the offer said how to accept`
        `excludes adjudication`                  IS `it excludes adjudication`
        `conditional`                            IS `it is conditional`
        `matter`                                 IS `my matter`
        `sets out the successful outcome`        IS `it defines success`
        `in clear plain language`                IS `it is in plain language`
        `signed by the client`                   IS `I signed it`
        `states the right to independent advice` IS `it mentions independent advice`
        `cooling-off business days`              IS `its cooling-off business days`
        `has an uplift fee`                      IS `it has an uplift fee`
        `uplift basis separately identified`     IS `the uplift basis is set out`
        `uplift estimated`                       IS `the uplift is estimated`
        `litigious`                              IS `my matter is litigious`
        `risk significant`                       IS `the risk is significant`
        `uplift fee`                             IS `the uplift fee`
        `costs otherwise payable`                IS `the costs otherwise payable`
        `contingency`                            IS `it is a share of what I recover`
        `adopts a scale`                         IS `it adopts an applicable scale`
        `client is sophisticated`                IS (`the kind of client I am` `with tender` `my costs were agreed by tender` `is a sophisticated client`))

@export Can I still end my no win, no fee (conditional) costs agreement in its cooling-off period (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cl 25(3)(e), (4), (5), (6))?
GIVEN `it is conditional`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement makes payment of some or all of the costs conditional on a successful outcome
      `the kind of client I am`         IS A `Kind of client` @desc What kind of client you are (an individual, a business or body not listed, or one of the large, professional or government clients the Act lists)
      `my costs were agreed by tender`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs, or their basis, were agreed through a tender process
      `it is between two law practices` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement is between your law practice and a law practice it retained for you (rather than with you)
      `its cooling-off business days`   IS A NUMBER  @desc How many clear business days of cooling-off the agreement gives; 0 if none
      `business days so far`            IS A NUMBER  @desc Counting from the first business day after the day you made the agreement up to today (today included if it is a business day), how many business days (not Saturdays, Sundays or public holidays) there have been
GIVETH A `Cooling-off answer`
`Can I still end my conditional costs agreement in the cooling-off period` MEANS
    `may I end the agreement in the cooling-off period (cl 25)` `it is conditional` ((`the kind of client I am` `with tender` `my costs were agreed by tender` `is a sophisticated client`) OR `it is between two law practices`) `its cooling-off business days` `business days so far`

@export My costs agreement is void: what is the most my law practice can recover from me (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cll 21, 29(2)-(5))?
GIVEN `why it is void`                    IS A `Why the agreement is void` @desc Why the agreement is void: it is a contingency fee agreement (cl 27); it breaches the uplift fee rules (cl 26); or it breaches another provision of Part 5
      `the fair amount`                   IS A NUMBER @desc The costs for the work under the applicable court scale or, if none, their fair and reasonable value, in dollars (as agreed or adjudicated)
      `the agreement amount without uplift` IS A NUMBER @desc What the agreement would have charged, without any uplift fee, in dollars
      `the uplift fee`                    IS A NUMBER @desc The uplift fee the agreement would have charged, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most my law practice may recover under my void costs agreement` MEANS
    `the most the law practice may recover under a void agreement (cl 29)` `why it is void` `the fair amount` `the agreement amount without uplift` `the uplift fee`

@export My costs agreement is void: how much must my law practice repay me (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cll 29(3)-(6))?
GIVEN `why it is void`                    IS A `Why the agreement is void` @desc Why the agreement is void: it is a contingency fee agreement (cl 27); it breaches the uplift fee rules (cl 26); or it breaches another provision of Part 5
      `the fair amount`                   IS A NUMBER @desc The costs for the work under the applicable court scale or, if none, their fair and reasonable value, in dollars
      `the agreement amount without uplift` IS A NUMBER @desc What the agreement would have charged, without any uplift fee, in dollars
      `the uplift fee`                    IS A NUMBER @desc The uplift fee the agreement would have charged, in dollars (0 if none)
      `what I have paid`                  IS A NUMBER @desc What you have paid the law practice for its services in the matter, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much must my law practice repay me under my void costs agreement` MEANS
    `the amount to be repaid under a void agreement (cl 29)` `why it is void` `the fair amount` `the agreement amount without uplift` `the uplift fee` `what I have paid`

@export Can I have my costs agreement set aside by the Supreme Court (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cll 18(3), 30)?
GIVEN `the court is satisfied it is unfair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court is satisfied that the agreement is not fair and reasonable (it may look at fraud or misrepresentation, missing disclosures, conduct before and after, and how the agreement deals with changed circumstances)
GIVETH A `Set aside answer`
`Can my costs agreement be set aside` MEANS
    `can the costs agreement be set aside (cl 30)` `the court is satisfied it is unfair`

@export If the Supreme Court sets aside my costs agreement, what is the most it can order me to pay (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cl 30(4)-(6))?
GIVEN `the court's figure`     IS A NUMBER @desc The costs the court fixes under the applicable scale or as fair and reasonable, in dollars
      `the agreement amount`   IS A NUMBER @desc What the law practice would have been entitled to recover under the agreement, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be ordered to pay after my costs agreement is set aside` MEANS
    `the most the court may order after setting aside (cl 30(6))` `the court's figure` `the agreement amount`

§§ `Interest on an unpaid bill (cl 23; reg 61)`
-- Situation: you have been given a bill and have not paid it.

@export Can my law practice charge me interest on my unpaid legal costs (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cl 23; Legal Practitioners Regulations 2014 reg 61)?
GIVEN `the bill states interest`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the bill contains a statement that interest is payable and of the rate
      `my costs agreement allows interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your costs agreement provides for interest on unpaid costs
      `the day of the bill`             IS A DATE    @desc The day the law practice gave you the bill
      `the day interest would start`    IS A DATE    @desc The day from which interest is being charged (or today)
      `the rate charged`                IS A NUMBER  @desc The interest rate charged, in per cent a year (for example 6.1)
      `the Cash Rate Target`            IS A NUMBER  @desc The Reserve Bank's Cash Rate Target on the day of the bill, in per cent (for example 4.1)
GIVETH AN `Interest answer`
`May my law practice charge me interest on unpaid costs` MEANS
    `may the law practice charge interest (cl 23)` `the bill states interest` `my costs agreement allows interest` `the day of the bill` `the day interest would start` `the rate charged` `the Cash Rate Target`

@export What is the highest interest rate my law practice may charge on my unpaid legal costs (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cl 23(4); Legal Practitioners Regulations 2014 reg 61)?
GIVEN `the Cash Rate Target` IS A NUMBER @desc The Reserve Bank's Cash Rate Target on the day the bill was issued, in per cent (for example 4.1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the highest interest rate my law practice may charge` MEANS
    `the highest interest rate (cl 23(4), reg 61)` `the Cash Rate Target`

§§ `Bills and being sued for costs (cll 18(2), 31, 34, 44)`
-- Situation: you have been given a bill, or the law practice wants to be paid.

@export By when must my law practice give me the itemised bill I asked for (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cl 34(2)); it may not charge for it (cl 34(6))?
GIVEN `the day I asked` IS A DATE @desc The day you asked for an itemised bill after receiving a lump sum bill
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I get the itemised bill I asked for` MEANS
    `the last day for the itemised bill (cl 34(2))` `the day I asked`

@export Did my law practice give me the itemised bill I asked for in time (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cl 34(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my bill was a lump sum bill`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the bill you were given was not itemised (a lump sum bill)
      `the day I asked`              IS A DATE    @desc The day you asked for an itemised bill
      `I have received it`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice has given you the itemised bill
      `the day I received it`        IS A DATE    @desc The day it gave you the itemised bill (any day if it has not)
      `today`                        IS A DATE    @desc Today's date
GIVETH AN `Itemised bill answer`
`Was my itemised bill given in time` MEANS
    `was the itemised bill given in time (cl 34)` `my bill was a lump sum bill` `the day I asked` `I have received it` `the day I received it` `today`

@export From what day may my law practice start court proceedings against me to recover its costs, counting the 30 days after the bill (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cll 31(1), 34(4), (5))?
GIVEN `the day of the bill`             IS A DATE    @desc The day the law practice gave you its bill
      `I asked for an itemised bill`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked for an itemised bill after a lump sum bill
      `the day I got the itemised bill` IS A DATE    @desc The day it gave you the itemised bill (any day if you did not ask)
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day may my law practice sue me for its costs` MEANS
    `the first day the law practice may sue (cll 31(1), 34(4), (5))` `the day of the bill` `I asked for an itemised bill` `the day I got the itemised bill`

@export May my law practice start (or have started) court proceedings against me to recover its costs on this day (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cll 18(2), 31, 34(4), (5), 44)?
GIVEN `it failed to disclose and the costs are not adjudicated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice failed to make a costs disclosure Part 3 required and the costs have not yet been adjudicated
      `my adjudication is pending`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an application for adjudication of these costs has been made and not yet completed
      `I was given a bill`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice has given you a signed bill with the statement of your rights
      `the day of the bill`             IS A DATE    @desc The day it gave you the bill
      `I asked for an itemised bill`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked for an itemised bill after a lump sum bill
      `I got the itemised bill`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it has given you the itemised bill you asked for
      `the day I got the itemised bill` IS A DATE    @desc The day it gave you the itemised bill (any day if not)
      `the court allowed it sooner`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court authorised earlier proceedings because you are about to leave South Australia
      `the day of the proceedings`      IS A DATE    @desc The day the proceedings were or would be started
GIVETH A `Proceedings answer`
`May my law practice sue me for its costs on this day` MEANS
    `may the law practice sue for its costs (cll 18(2), 31, 34, 44)` `it failed to disclose and the costs are not adjudicated` `my adjudication is pending` `I was given a bill` `the day of the bill` `I asked for an itemised bill` `I got the itemised bill` `the day I got the itemised bill` `the court allowed it sooner` `the day of the proceedings`

§§ `Having the costs adjudicated by the Supreme Court (Part 7)`
-- Situation: you dispute your law practice's costs.

@export By when must I apply to the Supreme Court for adjudication of my lawyer's costs (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cl 37(4))?
GIVEN `the day it runs from` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given the bill or asked to pay; or, if neither happened, the day you paid the costs
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply for adjudication of my lawyer's costs` MEANS
    `the last day to apply for adjudication (cl 37(4))` `the day it runs from`

@export Can my application for adjudication of my lawyer's costs be dealt with, given when I applied (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cll 37(4), (5), 51)?
GIVEN `the kind of client I am`        IS A `Kind of client` @desc What kind of client you are (an individual, a business or body not listed, or one of the large, professional or government clients the Act lists)
      `my costs were agreed by tender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs, or their basis, were agreed through a tender process
      `I contracted out`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you agreed with the law practice to contract out of adjudication (Part 7)
      `the day it runs from`           IS A DATE    @desc The day you were given the bill or asked to pay; or, if neither, the day you paid
      `I have applied`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied for adjudication
      `the day I applied`              IS A DATE    @desc The day you applied (any day if you have not)
      `today`                          IS A DATE    @desc Today's date
      `the court found it just and fair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has decided, given the delay and the reasons for it, that it is just and fair to deal with a late application (usually no, until it decides)
GIVETH AN `Adjudication time answer`
`Can my application for adjudication be dealt with` MEANS
    `can the application for adjudication be dealt with (cll 37, 51)` (`the kind of client I am` `with tender` `my costs were agreed by tender` `is a sophisticated client`) `I contracted out` `the day it runs from` `I have applied` `the day I applied` `today` `the court found it just and fair`

@export On adjudication, must the court measure my lawyer's costs by our costs agreement (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cl 47)?
GIVEN `it fixes the amount or a rate`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs agreement specifies the amount of these costs, or a rate or other way of calculating them
      `it was set aside`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement has been set aside under clause 30
      `the court finds it did not disclose properly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that the agreement does not comply in a material respect with the disclosure requirements of Part 3
      `the court finds Part 5 bars the costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that Part 5 (costs agreements) stops the law practice recovering these costs
      `we agreed otherwise`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the law practice agreed that the costs not be measured by the agreement
GIVETH AN `Agreement measure answer`
`Will the adjudication follow my costs agreement` MEANS
    `is the adjudication by the costs agreement (cl 47)` `it fixes the amount or a rate` `it was set aside` `the court finds it did not disclose properly` `the court finds Part 5 bars the costs` `we agreed otherwise`

@export Who pays the costs of the adjudication of my lawyer's bill (Legal Practitioners Act 1981 (SA) Schedule 3 cl 49)?
GIVEN `the costs billed`               IS A NUMBER  @desc The legal costs as billed, in dollars
      `the costs as adjudicated`       IS A NUMBER  @desc The legal costs as fixed by the adjudication, in dollars
      `the court finds a Part 3 failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that the law practice failed to comply with the costs disclosure rules (Part 3)
      `I applied`                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (rather than the law practice) applied for the adjudication
      `after the Commissioner decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied after the Legal Profession Conduct Commissioner made a determination about these costs (section 77N)
GIVETH AN `Adjudication costs answer`
`Who pays the costs of the adjudication` MEANS
    `who pays the costs of the adjudication (cl 49)` `the costs billed` `the costs as adjudicated` `the court finds a Part 3 failure` `I applied` `after the Commissioner decided`
